,"altText":"DEATHGASM 2: GOREMAGEDDON"},"posterImages":[{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/deathgasm-2-goremageddon/DEATHGASM-2-GOREMAGEDDON_sp-poster-copy.jpg?auto=compress&fit=clip&h=1620&q=80&w=1080","altText":"DEATHGASM 2: GOREMAGEDDON"}],"certification":"R"},"event":null,"eventType":null,"formatSlugs":["2d-digital"],"presentationAttributeSlugs":["advance-sales","first-run"],"associatedPresentationSlugs":[],"openingDateClt":"2026-09-29","openingDateDisplay":"Sep 29","superTitle":{"superTitle":"Fantastic Fest Presents","type":"COLLECTION","slug":"fantastic-fest-presents"},"isHidden":false,"primaryCollectionSlug":"fantastic-fest-presents","isAvailableForPersonalTheater":false},{"slug":"first-blood","legacySlug":null,"show":{"slug":"first-blood","legacySlug":null,"title":"First Blood","vistaHoCodes":["A000004396"],"headline":"Ted Kotcheff's genre-defining post-ROCKY masterpiece","landscapeHeroImage":{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/first-blood/First-Blood-still01.jpg?auto=compress&crop=focalpoint&fit=crop&fp-x=0.3829&fp-y=0.302&h=1080&q=80&w=1920","altText":"First Blood still01"},"portraitHeroImage":{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/first-blood/First-Blood-still01.jpg?auto=compress&crop=focalpoint&fit=crop&fp-x=0.3829&fp-y=0.302&h=1440&q=80&w=1080","altText":"First Blood still01"},"posterImages":[{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/first-blood/first-blood-poster.jpg?auto=compress&fit=clip&h=1620&q=80&w=1080","altText":"First blood poster"}],"certification":"R"},"event":null,"eventType":null,"formatSlugs":["2d-digital"],"presentationAttributeSlugs":["advance-sales","alamo-exclusive"],"associatedPresentationSlugs":[],"openingDateClt":"2026-09-12","openingDateDisplay":"Sep 12","superTitle":null,"isHidden":false,"primaryCollectionSlug":null,"isAvailableForPersonalTheater":false},{"slug":"special-event-star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan-space-seed","legacySlug":null,"show":{"slug":"star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan","legacySlug":null,"title":"Star Trek II: The Wrath of Khan","vistaHoCodes":["A000005101"],"headline":"The Starship Enterprise's most iconic cinematic adventure","landscapeHeroImage":{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan/STAR-TREK-II-THE-WRATH-OF-KHAN_hero.jpg?auto=compress&crop=focalpoint&fit=crop&fp-x=0.5&fp-y=0.5&h=1080&q=80&w=1920","altText":"STAR TREK II: THE WRATH OF KHAN"},"portraitHeroImage":{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan/STAR-TREK-II-THE-WRATH-OF-KHAN_portrait.jpg?auto=compress&crop=focalpoint&fit=crop&fp-x=0.5&fp-y=0.5&h=1440&q=80&w=1080","altText":"STAR TREK II: THE WRATH OF KHAN"},"posterImages":[{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/shows/star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan/STAR-TREK-II-THE-WRATH-OF-KHAN_sp-poster-copy.jpg?auto=compress&fit=clip&h=1620&q=80&w=1080","altText":"STAR TREK II: THE WRATH OF KHAN"}],"certification":"PG"},"event":{"slug":"special-event-star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan-space-seed","title":"<show-title>Star Trek II: The Wrath of Khan</show-title> <event-type-title>Director's Cut + \"Space Seed\"</event-type-title>","eventTypeSlug":"special-event","eventTypeTitleOverride":"Director's Cut + \"Space Seed\"","headline":"Paired with the TV episode that inspired the film, \"Space Seed\"","description":"<p><strong>About STAR TREK II: THE WRATH OF KHAN</strong><br />1982 | 113 mins.</p>\n<p>It is 1980. Disappointed with the performance of the decidedly un-STAR WARS-like results of STAR TREK: THE MOTION PICTURE, Paramount executives approach television producer Harve Bennett about taking over the next outing of the Starship Enterprise...but for a far lower budget than the prior film and its special effects extravaganza.</p>\n<p>To familiarize himself with the series, Bennett watched all 79 episodes of the original series, with one story – season one's \"Space Seed\" – igniting his imagination. The tale of an antiheroic superhuman named Khan who attempts to take over the Enterprise and who is left with his followers on an Earth-like planet to create their own utopia... well, it begged for a follow-up. Alongside co-writer Jack B. Sowards and young director Nicholas Meyer, Bennett created that follow-up, and set the stage for two more films that, though planned one-by-one, work as a perfect trilogy.</p>\n<p>An epic revenge tale that also manages to pack in meditations on aging, regret, and how we deal with death, it’s the finest moment in the entire original series canon, and (arguably) one of the greatest science-fiction films ever made.</p>\n<p><strong>About \"Space Seed\" (S1E22)</strong><br />1967 | 50 mins.</p>\n<p>While on patrol in deep space, Captain Kirk and his crew find and revive a genetically engineered world conqueror and his compatriots from Earth's twentieth century.</p>","vistaHoCodes":["A000036781"],"cinemaSessionIds":[],"landscapeHeroImage":null,"portraitHeroImage":null,"trailer":null,"posterImage":{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/events/special-event-star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan-space-seed/STAR-TREK-II-THE-WRATH-OF-KHAN-_Space-Seed__sp-poster-copy.jpg?auto=compress&fit=clip&h=1620&q=80&w=1080","altText":"STAR TREK II: THE WRATH OF KHAN Director's Cut + \"Space Seed\""},"additionalStillImages":[],"showSlug":"star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan","brandPriority":"BETTER","certification":"PG","runtimeMinutes":168,"includeShowDescription":false,"useDeluxeDescription":true,"contentBlocks":[{"contentBlockType":"paragraphs","paragraphs":"<p><strong>About STAR TREK II: THE WRATH OF KHAN</strong><br />1982 | 113 mins.</p>\n<p>It is 1980. Disappointed with the performance of the decidedly un-STAR WARS-like results of STAR TREK: THE MOTION PICTURE, Paramount executives approach television producer Harve Bennett about taking over the next outing of the Starship Enterprise...but for a far lower budget than the prior film and its special effects extravaganza.</p>\n<p>To familiarize himself with the series, Bennett watched all 79 episodes of the original series, with one story – season one's \"Space Seed\" – igniting his imagination. The tale of an antiheroic superhuman named Khan who attempts to take over the Enterprise and who is left with his followers on an Earth-like planet to create their own utopia... well, it begged for a follow-up. Alongside co-writer Jack B. Sowards and young director Nicholas Meyer, Bennett created that follow-up, and set the stage for two more films that, though planned one-by-one, work as a perfect trilogy.</p>\n<p>An epic revenge tale that also manages to pack in meditations on aging, regret, and how we deal with death, it’s the finest moment in the entire original series canon, and (arguably) one of the greatest science-fiction films ever made.</p>\n<p><strong>About \"Space Seed\" (S1E22)</strong><br />1967 | 50 mins.</p>\n<p>While on patrol in deep space, Captain Kirk and his crew find and revive a genetically engineered world conqueror and his compatriots from Earth's twentieth century.</p>"},{"contentBlockType":"image","alignment":"center","designAccent":false,"imageAsset":{"title":"Deluxe Showpage image 1920x1080","caption":null,"credit":[],"hideCredit":false,"official":false,"image":{"uri":"https://img-assets.drafthouse.com/images/events/special-event-star-trek-ii-the-wrath-of-khan-space-seed/Deluxe-Showpage-image_1920x1080.jpg?auto=compress&fit=clip&q=80","altText":"Deluxe Showpage image 1920x1080"}},"imageLink":null},{"contentBlockType":"paragraphs","paragraphs":"<p>Celebrate 60 years of Star Trek with an exclusive Alamo Drafthouse collection featuring two collectibles made for your next away mission. The 16 oz. <strong><a href=\"https://giftshop.drafthouse.com/products/star-trek-60th-anniversary-pint-glass\">Star Trek 60th Anniversary Pint Glass</a></strong>, featuring Spock, the Enterprise, and Starfleet insignia with art by Chris Bilheimer, is ready for your next toast. Plus, bri